{
  "version": "0.1.0",
  "note": "Reflect's nouns, in Naive's ontology format (Torian, 2026-11-19: Reflect's own copy, Naive's format). The top categories are Aristotle's ten Categories (Categories 4, 1b25-2a4), each mapped to a class of BFO (ISO/IEC 21838-2). A noun names what a record is about, not the record. Each noun names what it is a kind of in broader (SKOS broader): another noun or a top category, and every noun reaches exactly one top category. app is the life app a noun belongs to, or null when it is shared; kinds lists the life record kinds (app:kind in packages/core/src/life.ts) about it, and every kind is listed by exactly one noun. packages/core/src/terms/ontology.ts checks it.",
